From dbc963185e6164ed1873c7a7a517c12d1957a2ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 01:47:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AmgX: scaled right hand side, second review of the wrapper

- the convergence criteria of AmgX also stop when the norm of the
  residual is lower than 1e-20 (immediately if the norm of the initial
  residual is): without absolute tolerance, AmgXPCG multiplies the right
  hand side by a power of two giving it a norm between one and two, and
  the solution by its inverse (exact operations), so that its relative
  criterion does not depend on the scale of the right hand side; the
  preconditioner in single precision does the same with its default
  configuration, to stay in the range of the single precision; absolute
  tolerances lower than 1e-20 are refused
- options of a solver gathered in AmgXSolverOptions
- the collective checks of SetOperator throw a CollectiveFailure
- a resolution fails until AmgX gives its status (an exception left the
  status of the previous resolution)
- documentation of the floors of the convergence criteria
- tests: right hand sides multiplied by 1e-15, 1e-25, 1e-40 and 1e45 in
  double and single precision, zero right hand side, right hand side of
  invalid size, status after a failed resolution, absolute tolerance
  floor, message of the factory without GPU, synchronisation of the
  processes by point to point messages (a barrier could hide a
  collective destruction of the resources)
